hat the \"assessment\" is \"supported\". Yes.\n\nNow, we need to verify that the \"basis_refs\" includes all constraints. Yes.\n\nNow, we need to verify that the \"target\" matches the problem. Yes.\n\nThus the envelope is correct.\n\nNow, we need to ensure that we didn't include any extra whitespace or newlines? The JSON can have whitespace; it's fine. The output is raw JSON, can have formatting. Usually it's okay.\n\nNow, we need to ensure that we didn't include any extra fields beyond those required. The envelope includes \"candidate_tuples\" which is not in the template but is required per instruction. So it's okay.\n\nNow, we need to ensure that we didn't include any prose. So we output only the JSON.\n\nThus final answer is the JSON envelope.\n\nOne more check: The \"message_id\" is \"csp-5129-right-reviewer-1\". That matches the template. Good.\n\nNow, we need to ensure that the \"read_refs\" includes the correct reference. Yes.\n\nNow, we need to ensure that the \"recipients\" includes \"shared-integrator\". Yes.\n\nNow, we need to ensure that the \"reply_to\" is null. Yes.\n\nNow, we need to ensure that the \"schema_version\" is 1. Yes.\n\nNow, we need to ensure that the \"sender\" is \"right-reviewer\". Yes.\n\nNow, we need to ensure that the \"problem_id\" is \"csp-5129\". Yes.\n\nNow, we need to ensure that the \"payload.report\" includes \"assessment\", \"basis_refs\", \"candidate_tuples\", \"target\". Yes.\n\nNow, we need to ensure that the \"candidate_tuples\" is an array of arrays. Yes.\n\nNow, we need to ensure that the \"candidate_tuples\" includes the left component tuple. Yes.\n\nNow, we need to ensure that the \"candidate_tuples\" is in variable order a,b,c,d. Yes.\n\nNow, we need to ensure that the \"candidate_tuples\" is not empty. Yes.\n\nNow, we need to ensure that the \"candidate_tuples\" is a list of one tuple. Yes.\n\nNow, we need to ensure that the \"candidate_tuples\" is valid JSON. Yes.\n\nNow, we need to ensure that the \"basis_refs\"