         3,\n          2\n        ]\n      ],\n      \"target\": {\n        \"resource_id\": \"problem:csp-5129\",\n        \"revision\": 1,\n        \"state_revision\": 1\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"problem_id\": \"csp-5129\",\n  \"read_refs\": [\n    {\n      \"resource_id\": \"problem:csp-5129\",\n      \"revision\": 1,\n      \"state_revision\": 1\n    }\n  ],\n  \"recipients\": [\n    \"shared-integrator\"\n  ],\n  \"reply_to\": null,\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"sender\": \"right-reviewer\"\n}\n\nCheck for trailing commas: after \"candidate_tuples\" array, there is a comma before \"target\"? Yes, there is a comma after the candidate_tuples array. That's correct. After \"target\" object, there is a comma before closing of \"report\"? Yes. After \"read_refs\" array, there is a comma before \"recipients\"? Yes. After \"recipients\" array, there is a comma before \"reply_to\"? Yes. After \"reply_to\": null, there is a comma before \"schema_version\"? Yes. After \"schema_version\": 1, there is a comma before \"sender\"? Yes. So no trailing commas at the end of objects or arrays. Good.\n\nNow, we need to ensure that the \"candidate_tuples\" field is spelled exactly as expected. The instruction says \"candidate tuples\". It might be \"candidate_tuples\". Could also be \"candidate_tuples\". We'll assume that.\n\nNow, we need to ensure that the \"candidate_tuples\" contains the left component tuple. Yes.\n\nNow, we need to ensure that the \"candidate_tuples\" is a list of tuples. Yes.\n\nNow, we need to ensure that the \"candidate_tuples\" is in variable order. Yes.\n\nNow, we need to ensure that the \"candidate_tuples\" includes all satisfying tuples. Since there is only one, it's fine.\n\nNow, we need to ensure that the \"assessment\" is \"supported\". Yes.\n\nNow, we need to ensure that the \"basis_refs\" includes all constraints. Yes.\n\nNow, we need to ensure that the \"target\" matches the problem. Yes.\n\nThus the envelope is ready.\n\nNow, we need to output it